WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.904
In this video, we'll learn local frames,

00:00:02.904 --> 00:00:05.703
the coordinates every
weather station uses,

00:00:05.703 --> 00:00:08.502
and see how they're
used to follow the wind

00:00:08.502 --> 00:00:10.975
as the air moves over the round Earth.

00:00:11.775 --> 00:00:14.213
A forecaster at Brest, in France,

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:18.350
measures the wind with three
arrows: east, north and up.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:22.600
Are those the same three arrows
at Khulna, in Bangladesh?

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.900
And what happens to them as the air moves?

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.775
This is the fourth of seven
parts on coordinates.

00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:34.815
Now let's dive into local frames:
how they differ from place to place,

00:00:34.815 --> 00:00:40.175
how they turn by themselves as the air
moves, and why that matters for the wind.

00:00:40.975 --> 00:00:44.125
Now let's stand at a weather
station at Brest.

00:00:44.475 --> 00:00:47.534
Brest sits at the western tip of Brittany,

00:00:47.534 --> 00:00:51.175
in France, with the Atlantic
Ocean on three sides.

00:00:51.525 --> 00:00:55.850
A forecaster there doesn't use
axes from the Earth's centre.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:00.450
She uses three arrows of length
one, fixed to her own spot.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.425
I hat points east, j hat points north,

00:01:03.425 --> 00:01:07.500
and k hat points straight
up, away from the Earth's centre.

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:11.600
This is called the local
east, north, up frame.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:15.500
In Part 1, we called
the wind arrow bold u.

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:19.479
With three parts, it's usual
to call it bold v,

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:22.800
and to keep
small u, v and w for its parts.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:29.325
So the wind is u times i hat, plus
v times j hat, plus w times k hat.

00:01:29.675 --> 00:01:35.975
Here, u is the eastward wind, v the
northward wind, and w the upward wind.

00:01:36.325 --> 00:01:38.727
And i hat cross j hat is k hat,

00:01:38.727 --> 00:01:43.375
so the frame is right-handed,
as in the cross product movie.

00:01:43.725 --> 00:01:45.550
Why these arrows?

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:50.728
Gravity pulls along minus k hat, the
ground lies along i hat and

00:01:50.728 --> 00:01:54.575
j hat, and wind directions
are measured from north.

00:01:54.925 --> 00:01:58.100
So every weather report uses this frame.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:03.900
The next few steps write these three
arrows as numbers, one move at a time.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:07.300
They're here for anyone
who wants every step.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:11.658
You don't need them to follow
the weather, the climate or maps,

00:02:11.658 --> 00:02:15.475
so if it feels like a lot, skip
ahead to the time on screen.

00:02:15.825 --> 00:02:21.492
Each of the three arrows can be written
with the Earth's fixed axes from Part 3:

00:02:21.492 --> 00:02:23.829
x hat points to latitude zero and

00:02:23.829 --> 00:02:26.167
longitude zero, y hat to latitude

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:30.275
zero and ninety degrees
east, and z hat to the North Pole.

00:02:30.625 --> 00:02:33.875
Let's start with up,
because it's the easiest.

00:02:34.225 --> 00:02:37.050
Up points straight out
from the Earth's centre.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:42.346
That's exactly the direction of the arrow
from the centre to the station,

00:02:42.346 --> 00:02:44.175
the one we found in Part 3.

00:02:44.525 --> 00:02:49.325
So k hat is cosine phi cosine
lambda, cosine phi sine lambda,

00:02:49.325 --> 00:02:54.125
sine phi, where phi is the latitude
and lambda the longitude.

00:02:55.625 --> 00:02:57.950
Let's put in Brest's numbers.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:01.732
Brest is at forty
eight point four degrees north,

00:03:01.732 --> 00:03:07.125
and four point five degrees west, so
lambda is minus four point five degrees.

00:03:07.475 --> 00:03:13.775
Cosine phi is zero point six six four, and
sine phi is zero point seven four eight.

00:03:14.125 --> 00:03:17.425
Cosine lambda
is zero point nine nine seven,

00:03:17.425 --> 00:03:21.400
and sine lambda is minus
zero point zero seven eight.

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:26.072
The first part of k hat is cosine
phi times cosine lambda,

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:29.350
which comes to about
zero point six six two.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:32.893
The second, cosine phi times sine lambda,

00:03:32.893 --> 00:03:36.475
comes to about
minus zero point zero five two.

00:03:36.825 --> 00:03:40.000
And the third
is zero point seven four eight.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:47.450
Its length is one, because it's still the
arrow from Part 3, divided by the radius.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:49.825
Now east.

00:03:50.175 --> 00:03:54.050
Let's look down on the Earth
from far above the North Pole.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.763
From there, the circle
of latitude through Brest,

00:03:57.763 --> 00:04:01.125
the parallel, is a circle
round the Earth's axis.

00:04:01.475 --> 00:04:05.245
Brest sits on it at the angle
lambda from the x axis,

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:09.300
measured anticlockwise as seen
from above the North Pole.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:15.625
Going east means lambda grows, so Brest
slides anticlockwise round this circle.

00:04:15.975 --> 00:04:19.175
This is exactly the picture from Part 1.

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:22.414
The arrow pointing
from the circle's centre

00:04:22.414 --> 00:04:24.900
out to Brest plays the role of r hat.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:30.277
We'll call it capital R hat: it points
straight away from the Earth's axis,

00:04:30.277 --> 00:04:34.700
level with the equator,
and it's cosine lambda, sine lambda, zero.

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:40.200
East is the way the angle grows, so
east plays the role of theta hat.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:46.369
In Part 1, we found theta hat by turning
r hat by ninety degrees anticlockwise:

00:04:46.369 --> 00:04:50.125
swap the two numbers,
and put a minus on the first.

00:04:50.475 --> 00:04:54.250
So i hat is minus sine
lambda, cosine lambda.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:58.174
Its third part is zero,
because east runs level,

00:04:58.174 --> 00:05:01.600
round the circle, with no
part along the axis.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:08.850
At Brest, that's zero point zero seven
eight, zero point nine nine seven, zero.

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:14.750
So east at Brest points
almost exactly along y hat.

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:18.763
That makes sense: Brest
is close to longitude zero,

00:05:18.763 --> 00:05:22.425
and there, east points
towards ninety degrees east.

00:05:23.225 --> 00:05:24.750
Now north.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:29.087
This time, let's slice the Earth
along Brest's meridian,

00:05:29.087 --> 00:05:34.000
the half circle from pole to pole
through Brest, as we did in Part 3.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:38.600
In this slice, there are two
fixed directions: capital R hat,

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:42.850
pointing away from the axis, and z hat,
pointing up the axis.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:47.925
Up, k hat, sits at the angle
phi above capital R hat.

00:05:48.275 --> 00:05:50.726
So, just like r hat in Part 1,

00:05:50.726 --> 00:05:56.200
k hat is cosine phi times
capital R hat, plus sine phi times z hat.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:03.525
North is the way phi grows: Brest sliding
round the meridian towards the North Pole.

00:06:03.875 --> 00:06:07.400
So north plays the role
of theta hat in this slice.

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:11.238
Let's turn k hat by ninety
degrees towards the pole,

00:06:11.238 --> 00:06:16.000
with the same rule: swap the two numbers,
and put a minus on the first.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:21.250
That gives j hat equals minus sine
phi times capital R hat,

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:23.575
plus cosine phi times z hat.

00:06:23.925 --> 00:06:29.400
Now put in capital R hat, which
is cosine lambda, sine lambda, zero.

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:36.325
So j hat is minus sine phi cosine lambda,
minus sine phi sine lambda, cosine phi.

00:06:37.825 --> 00:06:41.742
At Brest, that's
minus zero point seven four five,

00:06:41.742 --> 00:06:46.050
zero point zero five nine, and
zero point six six four.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:53.075
So north at Brest points partly up the
Earth's axis, and partly in towards it.

00:06:53.875 --> 00:06:59.000
Let's check that these really are three
arrows of length one, at right angles.

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:04.000
For i hat, the squares of its east
and north parts add up to one.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:10.574
Next, the dot product of i hat and j hat:
we multiply their first parts,

00:07:10.574 --> 00:07:14.450
their second parts and their
third parts, and add them.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:17.575
That gives zero, up to rounding.

00:07:17.925 --> 00:07:20.000
So they're at right angles.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.200
The other pairs work out the same way.

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:30.742
And with the cross product recipe, i hat
cross j hat gives zero point six six two,

00:07:30.742 --> 00:07:35.575
minus zero point zero five two, and
zero point seven four eight.

00:07:35.925 --> 00:07:37.675
That's k hat.

00:07:39.175 --> 00:07:42.421
So the three local
arrows are right-handed,

00:07:42.421 --> 00:07:46.875
just like x hat, y hat
and z hat, only turned to fit Brest.

00:07:47.225 --> 00:07:52.013
If you skipped, here's what to keep:
every place has its own three arrows,

00:07:52.013 --> 00:07:57.125
east, north and up, and up always points
straight away from the Earth's centre.

00:07:57.925 --> 00:08:00.450
Each station has its own frame.

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:03.550
Let's zoom back out to the whole globe.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:08.975
Trappes, near Paris, is four hundred
and eighty kilometres east of Brest.

00:08:09.325 --> 00:08:11.300
How different is its up?

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:17.350
The angle between two ups is the angle at
the Earth's centre between the two places.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:22.475
By the arc rule, that's the distance
divided by the Earth's radius.

00:08:22.825 --> 00:08:28.325
That's zero point zero seven five radians,
about four point three degrees.

00:08:29.825 --> 00:08:32.475
Now Singapore, near the equator.

00:08:32.825 --> 00:08:36.675
For places far apart, the
dot product is easier.

00:08:37.025 --> 00:08:39.978
The dot product of two
arrows of length one

00:08:39.978 --> 00:08:42.725
is the cosine of the angle between them.

00:08:43.075 --> 00:08:46.837
Singapore's up is minus
zero point two three nine,

00:08:46.837 --> 00:08:50.750
zero point nine seven
one, zero point zero two four.

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:54.950
Multiply the matching parts
of the two ups, and add.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:59.825
Those three products add up
to minus zero point one nine one.

00:09:01.325 --> 00:09:03.249
The angle whose cosine is

00:09:03.249 --> 00:09:08.250
minus zero point one nine one
is about a hundred and one degrees.

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:14.125
So Singapore's up points more
than a right angle away from Brest's up.

00:09:14.925 --> 00:09:18.875
Now let's fly to Khulna, in
south-west Bangladesh.

00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:22.410
Khulna lies on the rivers
of the Ganges delta,

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:27.325
just north of the Sundarbans,
the largest mangrove forest in the world.

00:09:27.675 --> 00:09:31.374
To the south is the Bay
of Bengal, and to the west,

00:09:31.374 --> 00:09:34.275
across the border, is Kolkata, in India.

00:09:34.625 --> 00:09:39.743
In May twenty twenty, the centre
of Cyclone Amphan, which we met in Part 2,

00:09:39.743 --> 00:09:43.291
passed about seventy nine
kilometres west of Khulna,

00:09:43.291 --> 00:09:46.225
and the sea flooded
the coast to its south.

00:09:46.575 --> 00:09:49.890
Khulna is at twenty
two point eight degrees north,

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:52.475
and eighty nine point six degrees east.

00:09:52.825 --> 00:09:56.021
There, cosine phi
is zero point nine two two,

00:09:56.021 --> 00:09:58.719
sine phi zero point three eight eight,

00:09:58.719 --> 00:10:01.843
cosine lambda
zero point zero zero seven and

00:10:01.843 --> 00:10:07.240
sine lambda almost exactly one, so
its up arrow is zero point zero zero six,

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:11.075
zero point nine two
two, zero point three eight eight.

00:10:12.575 --> 00:10:17.775
Dotted with Brest's up, part by part, that
gives zero point two four six.

00:10:18.125 --> 00:10:19.945
The angle whose cosine is

00:10:19.945 --> 00:10:24.750
zero point two four six is about
seventy five point eight degrees.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:28.400
Even east is different.

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:33.451
Khulna's i hat is minus
one, zero point zero zero seven,

00:10:33.451 --> 00:10:36.725
zero, almost exactly opposite to x hat.

00:10:37.075 --> 00:10:40.550
It's about ninety four degrees
away from Brest's east.

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:45.816
So forecasters in Khulna
and in Brest both say east,

00:10:45.816 --> 00:10:49.075
north and up, but they
mean different arrows.

00:10:49.425 --> 00:10:51.450
Let's zoom back out.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:57.100
Sometimes a forecaster turns her
east and north arrows on purpose.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:11:02.417
On a coast, what matters is the part
of the wind blowing along the shore,

00:11:02.417 --> 00:11:06.500
and the part blowing across
it, onto the land or out to sea.

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:11.912
We did exactly this in Part 2, for
Hurricane Ian at Fort Myers Beach,

00:11:11.912 --> 00:11:16.975
on the south-west coast of Florida,
with the turned axes from Part 1.

00:11:17.325 --> 00:11:20.066
The new along arrow, x hat prime,

00:11:20.066 --> 00:11:24.800
is cosine alpha times i hat, plus sine
alpha times j hat.

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:31.000
The new across arrow, y hat prime, is that
one turned by ninety degrees:

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:35.875
minus sine alpha times i hat, plus cosine
alpha times j hat.

00:11:36.225 --> 00:11:41.069
The coast there runs at a bearing
of three hundred and twenty nine degrees,

00:11:41.069 --> 00:11:44.040
so alpha was a hundred
and twenty one degrees,

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:46.300
and y hat prime pointed out to sea.

00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:48.765
Then Ian's wind split into about

00:11:48.765 --> 00:11:52.069
nine point four metres
per second along the shore,

00:11:52.069 --> 00:11:57.025
and about minus thirty one and a half
across it, which means onto the land.

00:11:57.375 --> 00:12:02.850
In three dimensions, there's one more
arrow: we keep up, k hat, as it is,

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:06.600
and turn only i hat
and j hat, by the angle alpha,

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:09.075
anticlockwise as seen from above.

00:12:09.425 --> 00:12:14.645
One question was left open in Part 2:
the coast's two legs, ninety one and

00:12:14.645 --> 00:12:18.524
a half kilometres north
and fifty five kilometres west,

00:12:18.524 --> 00:12:21.275
were read off a flat map in kilometres.

00:12:21.625 --> 00:12:25.625
Now we can work them out
from latitude and longitude.

00:12:26.425 --> 00:12:29.650
First, we need two
points on the coastline.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.716
Let's take one near Naples, in Florida,

00:12:32.716 --> 00:12:35.920
at twenty six point one zero
degrees north and

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:38.775
eighty one point eight zero degrees west.

00:12:39.125 --> 00:12:42.159
And one near Englewood,
further up the coast,

00:12:42.159 --> 00:12:45.261
at twenty six point nine two
degrees north and

00:12:45.261 --> 00:12:48.025
eighty two point three five degrees west.

00:12:48.375 --> 00:12:51.450
Both come from a world map of coastlines.

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:53.984
Going from Naples to Englewood,

00:12:53.984 --> 00:12:58.000
the latitude grows by
zero point eight two three degrees.

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:04.425
The longitude changes by minus
zero point five five three degrees.

00:13:04.775 --> 00:13:07.425
It's minus because we go west.

00:13:08.925 --> 00:13:14.100
Now let's turn these angles into
kilometres, with the rules from Part 3.

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:20.150
The step north is the Earth's radius
times the change in latitude, in radians.

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:24.643
One degree is zero point zero
one seven four five radians,

00:13:24.643 --> 00:13:27.500
so zero point eight two three degrees is

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:30.571
zero point zero one
four three six radians,

00:13:30.571 --> 00:13:33.714
and the step north
is the radius times that:

00:13:33.714 --> 00:13:36.500
about ninety one and a half kilometres.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:41.609
The step east
is the radius, times cosine phi,

00:13:41.609 --> 00:13:44.825
times the change in longitude in radians.

00:13:45.175 --> 00:13:48.722
For phi, we use the middle
latitude, twenty six and

00:13:48.722 --> 00:13:52.825
a half degrees, whose cosine
is zero point eight nine five.

00:13:53.175 --> 00:13:55.358
With the change in longitude,

00:13:55.358 --> 00:14:00.177
minus zero point zero zero nine six five
radians, the step east,

00:14:00.177 --> 00:14:03.113
the radius times cosine phi times that,

00:14:03.113 --> 00:14:06.350
comes to about minus fifty
five kilometres.

00:14:07.850 --> 00:14:11.389
So going up the coast, we
move about ninety one and

00:14:11.389 --> 00:14:15.275
a half kilometres north, and fifty
five kilometres west.

00:14:15.625 --> 00:14:20.567
These are the two legs Part 2 used
for the coast's bearing: their ratio,

00:14:20.567 --> 00:14:24.823
zero point six zero one, is the
tangent of thirty one degrees,

00:14:24.823 --> 00:14:28.324
so the coast runs thirty
one degrees west of north,

00:14:28.324 --> 00:14:31.825
a bearing of three hundred
and twenty nine degrees.

00:14:33.325 --> 00:14:35.700
Now a second kind of turning.

00:14:36.050 --> 00:14:40.900
Our arrows also turn by themselves,
as you move over the round Earth.

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:45.392
Suppose a plane flies due east
along the parallel through Brest,

00:14:45.392 --> 00:14:48.175
at two hundred and fifty
metres per second.

00:14:48.525 --> 00:14:52.596
In one hour, which is three
thousand six hundred seconds,

00:14:52.596 --> 00:14:55.025
it covers nine hundred kilometres.

00:14:56.525 --> 00:14:58.071
As we found in Part 3,

00:14:58.071 --> 00:15:02.708
at Brest one degree of longitude
is about seventy four kilometres,

00:15:02.708 --> 00:15:05.800
so that's about twelve
degrees of longitude.

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:12.736
Seen from above the North Pole, the plane
has gone twelve degrees round the axis,

00:15:12.736 --> 00:15:16.897
and its east arrow has swung
round by the same twelve degrees,

00:15:16.897 --> 00:15:19.850
just like theta hat
swinging round a circle.

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:22.750
Going north tips the arrows too.

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:26.218
After a hundred and eleven
kilometres north,

00:15:26.218 --> 00:15:31.250
which is one degree of latitude,
the up arrow has tilted by one degree.

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:37.025
So for a moving air parcel, i hat, j hat
and k hat keep changing.

00:15:37.375 --> 00:15:42.625
We write their rates of change
as capital D i hat by D t, and so on.

00:15:42.975 --> 00:15:48.511
Capital D by D t means the rate
of change as we follow the air parcel,

00:15:48.511 --> 00:15:50.725
as in the derivatives movie.

00:15:51.075 --> 00:15:54.375
How fast do the arrows
turn, and which way?

00:15:54.725 --> 00:15:57.800
Let's work it out, one motion at a time.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:02.375
Now let's work out exactly
how fast the arrows turn.

00:16:02.725 --> 00:16:06.100
This part is for those
who enjoy every step.

00:16:06.450 --> 00:16:09.913
It isn't needed for the weather,
the climate or maps,

00:16:09.913 --> 00:16:13.050
so skip ahead to the time
on screen if you like.

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:16.225
We need just two results from Part 2.

00:16:16.575 --> 00:16:21.570
Take a point going round a circle, with
r hat pointing out from the centre,

00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:24.700
and theta hat pointing
the way the angle grows.

00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:29.723
First, as the angle grows, r hat
changes towards theta hat,

00:16:29.723 --> 00:16:33.050
and theta hat changes towards minus r hat.

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:37.870
We wrote that as d r hat by d theta
equals theta hat,

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:41.750
and d theta hat by d theta
equals minus r hat.

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:47.536
Second, if the point moves
along the circle at a speed v,

00:16:47.536 --> 00:16:53.175
its angle grows at v divided by the
circle's radius, in radians per second.

00:16:53.525 --> 00:16:58.338
Putting the two together with the chain
rule from the derivatives movie,

00:16:58.338 --> 00:17:02.750
theta hat changes at minus r hat, times
the speed over the radius.

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:07.950
And r hat changes at theta
hat, times the speed over the radius.

00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:11.625
So here's the recipe.

00:17:11.975 --> 00:17:15.407
Find the circle, find
which arrow plays r hat and

00:17:15.407 --> 00:17:20.100
which plays theta hat, and divide
the speed by the circle's radius.

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:25.550
An air parcel can move in three
ways: east, north and up.

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:29.875
Let's take them one
at a time, and add them up at the end.

00:17:30.225 --> 00:17:32.700
Going straight up is the easiest.

00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:36.448
Look at our three formulas:
i hat, j hat and

00:17:36.448 --> 00:17:41.700
k hat depend only on phi and
lambda, the latitude and the longitude.

00:17:42.050 --> 00:17:46.500
Going up changes neither,
so going up turns none of the arrows.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:51.350
Going north changes phi, but not lambda.

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:56.875
And i hat, minus sine lambda, cosine
lambda, zero, has no phi in it.

00:17:57.225 --> 00:18:00.000
So going north leaves i hat alone.

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:05.979
That leaves four things to find:
how going east turns i hat,

00:18:05.979 --> 00:18:11.950
how going north turns j hat and k hat, and
how going east turns j hat and k hat.

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:15.550
First, going east, and i hat.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:21.698
Going east, the parcel moves round its
parallel: a circle round the Earth's axis,

00:18:21.698 --> 00:18:27.425
whose radius is the distance from the
axis, the Earth's radius times cosine phi.

00:18:27.775 --> 00:18:32.579
In the view from above the North
Pole, capital R hat plays r hat,

00:18:32.579 --> 00:18:36.275
i hat plays theta hat, and lambda
plays the angle.

00:18:36.625 --> 00:18:39.600
First, how fast does lambda grow?

00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:42.574
The parcel moves east at the speed u,

00:18:42.574 --> 00:18:47.325
round a circle whose radius
is the Earth's radius times cosine phi.

00:18:47.675 --> 00:18:51.575
So lambda grows
at u divided by that radius.

00:18:53.075 --> 00:18:57.925
Next, Part 2's rule says theta hat
changes towards minus r hat.

00:18:58.275 --> 00:19:03.281
So as lambda grows, i hat changes
towards minus capital R hat:

00:19:03.281 --> 00:19:07.075
d i hat by d lambda equals
minus capital R hat.

00:19:08.575 --> 00:19:11.775
Now multiply the two, by the chain rule.

00:19:12.125 --> 00:19:16.388
Capital D i hat by D t equals
minus capital R hat,

00:19:16.388 --> 00:19:20.650
times u, over the Earth's
radius times cosine phi.

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:27.550
In words: going east, the east arrow
swings in towards the Earth's axis.

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:31.975
But a forecaster doesn't
use capital R hat.

00:19:32.325 --> 00:19:35.050
She wants the answer in her own arrows.

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:38.450
Let's go back to Brest's meridian slice.

00:19:38.800 --> 00:19:44.450
There, we wrote k hat as cosine phi
capital R hat, plus sine phi z hat.

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:50.325
And j hat as minus sine phi
capital R hat, plus cosine phi z hat.

00:19:50.675 --> 00:19:56.725
Next, multiply the first line by cosine
phi, and the second line by sine phi.

00:19:57.075 --> 00:20:00.275
Then take the second
line away from the first.

00:20:00.625 --> 00:20:02.479
The z hat parts cancel,

00:20:02.479 --> 00:20:07.475
because cosine phi sine phi
minus sine phi cosine phi is zero.

00:20:07.825 --> 00:20:11.037
The capital R hat parts
give cosine squared

00:20:11.037 --> 00:20:14.025
phi plus sine squared phi, which is one.

00:20:14.375 --> 00:20:19.925
So capital R hat equals cosine
phi k hat, minus sine phi j hat.

00:20:21.425 --> 00:20:26.650
In words: pointing away from the axis
is partly up, and partly south.

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:32.700
Now put minus capital R hat into the
chain-rule result we found a moment ago.

00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:39.302
Capital D i hat by D t equals u over
the Earth's radius times cosine phi,

00:20:39.302 --> 00:20:45.725
times, open bracket, j hat sine phi, minus
k hat cosine phi, close bracket.

00:20:47.225 --> 00:20:51.219
So going east, the east arrow
tips a little towards the north,

00:20:51.219 --> 00:20:52.700
and a little downwards.

00:20:53.050 --> 00:20:54.625
How fast?

00:20:54.975 --> 00:20:59.165
For a wind of ten metres per second
towards the east at Brest,

00:20:59.165 --> 00:21:01.936
divide ten by the distance from the axis,

00:21:01.936 --> 00:21:05.450
four million two hundred
and thirty thousand metres.

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:11.025
That's about two point four times ten
to the minus six radians per second.

00:21:12.525 --> 00:21:15.225
That's about twelve degrees in a day.

00:21:16.025 --> 00:21:19.975
Next, going north, which
turns j hat and k hat.

00:21:20.325 --> 00:21:23.728
Going north, the parcel
moves round its meridian:

00:21:23.728 --> 00:21:29.075
a circle round the Earth's centre, whose
radius is the Earth's radius itself.

00:21:29.425 --> 00:21:34.800
In the meridian slice, k hat points
out from the centre, so it plays r hat.

00:21:35.150 --> 00:21:39.575
And j hat points the way phi
grows, so it plays theta hat.

00:21:39.925 --> 00:21:45.425
The parcel moves north at the speed v, so
phi grows at v over the radius.

00:21:46.925 --> 00:21:50.450
Part 2's rules then
give the answer at once.

00:21:50.800 --> 00:21:53.246
K hat changes towards j hat:

00:21:53.246 --> 00:21:58.050
capital D k hat
by D t equals j hat, v over the radius.

00:21:58.400 --> 00:22:01.749
And j hat changes towards minus k hat:

00:22:01.749 --> 00:22:07.125
capital D j hat by D t equals
minus k hat, v over the radius.

00:22:08.625 --> 00:22:13.875
In words: going north, up tips towards
the north, and north tips downwards.

00:22:14.225 --> 00:22:18.748
A hundred and eleven kilometres
north, over the Earth's radius,

00:22:18.748 --> 00:22:22.194
is about
zero point zero one seven five radians:

00:22:22.194 --> 00:22:25.425
the one-degree tilt
of up that we saw before.

00:22:26.925 --> 00:22:30.900
Last, going east also
tilts j hat and k hat.

00:22:31.250 --> 00:22:36.606
Look again at how they're built:
k hat is cosine phi capital R hat,

00:22:36.606 --> 00:22:41.641
plus sine phi z hat, and j hat
is minus sine phi capital R hat,

00:22:41.641 --> 00:22:43.400
plus cosine phi z hat.

00:22:43.750 --> 00:22:49.000
Going east, phi stays the same, so
the sines and cosines don't change.

00:22:49.350 --> 00:22:53.500
Z hat lies along the Earth's
axis, and never turns.

00:22:53.850 --> 00:22:56.350
Only capital R hat turns.

00:22:56.700 --> 00:23:00.413
In the view from above,
capital R hat plays r hat,

00:23:00.413 --> 00:23:04.200
so it changes towards i hat, which
plays theta hat.

00:23:04.550 --> 00:23:08.323
Capital D capital R hat
by D t equals i hat,

00:23:08.323 --> 00:23:12.525
times u over the Earth's
radius times cosine phi.

00:23:14.025 --> 00:23:18.475
So capital D k hat by D t is cosine
phi times that.

00:23:18.825 --> 00:23:23.300
The cosines cancel,
leaving i hat, u over the radius.

00:23:24.800 --> 00:23:30.214
And capital D j hat by D t is minus sine
phi times the same thing:

00:23:30.214 --> 00:23:35.875
minus i hat, times u over the
radius, times sine phi over cosine phi.

00:23:36.225 --> 00:23:38.783
Sine over cosine is the tangent,

00:23:38.783 --> 00:23:43.100
so that's minus i hat, u over the radius,
tangent phi.

00:23:44.600 --> 00:23:50.400
In words: going east, up leans towards the
east, and north leans towards the west.

00:23:51.200 --> 00:23:53.425
Now let's add the motions.

00:23:53.775 --> 00:23:58.225
In a short time, the parcel
moves a little east and a little north.

00:23:58.575 --> 00:24:02.265
As in the total differential
from the derivatives movie,

00:24:02.265 --> 00:24:04.900
the small changes from each move add up.

00:24:05.250 --> 00:24:11.147
So capital D i hat by D t equals u over
the radius times cosine phi,

00:24:11.147 --> 00:24:17.650
times, open bracket, j hat sine phi, minus
k hat cosine phi, close bracket.

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:23.388
Capital D j hat by D t equals
minus i hat, u over the radius,

00:24:23.388 --> 00:24:27.275
tangent phi, minus k hat, v over
the radius.

00:24:27.625 --> 00:24:31.131
And capital D k hat by D t equals i hat,

00:24:31.131 --> 00:24:35.425
u over the radius, plus j hat, v over
the radius.

00:24:36.925 --> 00:24:40.243
Every piece is a speed
divided by a radius,

00:24:40.243 --> 00:24:43.175
just as round the hurricane in Part 2.

00:24:43.525 --> 00:24:47.075
Speed over radius
is how fast the arrows turn.

00:24:47.425 --> 00:24:49.225
And here's a check.

00:24:49.575 --> 00:24:55.560
The change of i hat has no i hat part, the
change of j hat has no j hat part,

00:24:55.560 --> 00:24:58.825
and the change of k hat has no k hat part.

00:24:59.175 --> 00:25:01.075
That has to be so.

00:25:01.425 --> 00:25:04.976
An arrow of length one
can only turn, never grow,

00:25:04.976 --> 00:25:08.600
so its change is always
at right angles to itself.

00:25:10.100 --> 00:25:13.500
No earlier movie derived
these three lines.

00:25:13.850 --> 00:25:17.032
The cross product at work
met a close cousin:

00:25:17.032 --> 00:25:21.700
an arrow carried round by a spin
changes at Omega cross the arrow.

00:25:22.050 --> 00:25:24.548
These three lines follow the same rule,

00:25:24.548 --> 00:25:28.200
with the flow's own turning
in place of the Earth's spin.

00:25:28.550 --> 00:25:34.002
If you skipped, here's what to keep: as
air moves over the round Earth, its east,

00:25:34.002 --> 00:25:39.050
north and up arrows turn, at about
its speed divided by the Earth's radius.

00:25:39.850 --> 00:25:41.775
Why does all this matter?

00:25:42.125 --> 00:25:44.225
Because of Newton's law.

00:25:44.575 --> 00:25:48.700
The next three steps show where
the turning arrows end up in it.

00:25:49.050 --> 00:25:51.525
They're for anyone who wants every step,

00:25:51.525 --> 00:25:54.804
and you don't need them
for the intuition of weather,

00:25:54.804 --> 00:25:58.825
climate or maps, so skip ahead
to the time on screen if you like.

00:25:59.175 --> 00:26:01.891
Force equals mass times acceleration,

00:26:01.891 --> 00:26:06.808
and the acceleration is the rate
of change of the whole wind arrow,

00:26:06.808 --> 00:26:09.450
bold v, as we follow the air parcel.

00:26:09.800 --> 00:26:14.775
Bold v is u i hat, plus v
j hat, plus w k hat.

00:26:15.125 --> 00:26:18.045
Each of those is a number times an arrow,

00:26:18.045 --> 00:26:21.250
and as the parcel
moves, both of them change.

00:26:21.600 --> 00:26:24.600
So we need the product rule from Part 2.

00:26:24.950 --> 00:26:30.107
The change of a number times an arrow is
the change of the number times the arrow,

00:26:30.107 --> 00:26:33.000
plus the number times
the change of the arrow.

00:26:34.500 --> 00:26:37.850
Using it on all three
pieces gives six terms.

00:26:38.200 --> 00:26:44.115
Capital D bold v by D t equals
capital D u by D t times i hat,

00:26:44.115 --> 00:26:47.550
plus u times capital D i hat by D t.

00:26:47.900 --> 00:26:54.425
Plus capital D v by D t times j
hat, plus v times capital D j hat by D t.

00:26:54.775 --> 00:26:58.375
Plus capital D w by D t times k hat,

00:26:58.375 --> 00:27:01.975
plus w times capital D k hat by D t.

00:27:03.475 --> 00:27:07.217
In each pair, the first term
is the change of the number,

00:27:07.217 --> 00:27:09.975
and the second is the change of the arrow.

00:27:10.775 --> 00:27:14.400
Let's find the eastward
part of this acceleration.

00:27:14.750 --> 00:27:18.050
How do we get the part
of any arrow along i hat?

00:27:18.400 --> 00:27:21.500
With the dot product, as in Part 1.

00:27:21.850 --> 00:27:25.875
So we dot all six terms
with i hat, one at a time.

00:27:26.225 --> 00:27:31.100
First term:
capital D u by D t, times i hat dot i hat.

00:27:31.450 --> 00:27:35.875
I hat dot i hat is one, so
it's capital D u by D t.

00:27:37.375 --> 00:27:42.475
Second term:
u times capital D i hat by D t, dot i hat.

00:27:42.825 --> 00:27:45.814
The change of i hat has only j hat and

00:27:45.814 --> 00:27:49.825
k hat parts, and both are
at right angles to i hat.

00:27:50.175 --> 00:27:52.225
So this term is zero.

00:27:53.725 --> 00:27:58.725
Third term:
capital D v by D t, times j hat dot i hat.

00:27:59.075 --> 00:28:03.500
J hat is at right angles
to i hat, so that's zero too.

00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:09.314
Fifth term, in the same way:
capital D w by D t,

00:28:09.314 --> 00:28:12.100
times k hat dot i hat, is zero.

00:28:13.600 --> 00:28:16.075
Now the two terms that survive.

00:28:16.425 --> 00:28:21.375
Fourth term:
v times capital D j hat by D t, dot i hat.

00:28:21.725 --> 00:28:28.110
Capital D j hat by D t has an i hat
part, minus u over the radius tangent phi,

00:28:28.110 --> 00:28:31.875
and a k hat part, which
the dot product drops.

00:28:32.225 --> 00:28:37.154
So this term is v times
minus u over the radius tangent phi:

00:28:37.154 --> 00:28:40.275
minus u v tangent phi over the radius.

00:28:41.775 --> 00:28:47.050
Sixth term:
w times capital D k hat by D t, dot i hat.

00:28:47.400 --> 00:28:52.525
Capital D k hat by D t has
the i hat part, u over the radius.

00:28:52.875 --> 00:28:56.425
So this term is plus u w over the radius.

00:28:57.925 --> 00:28:59.790
Adding the six terms,

00:28:59.790 --> 00:29:05.117
capital D bold v by D t dot i hat
equals capital D u by D t,

00:29:05.117 --> 00:29:10.800
minus u v tangent phi over the
radius, plus u w over the radius.

00:29:12.300 --> 00:29:15.900
The first term is the change
of the number u.

00:29:16.250 --> 00:29:20.825
The other two come only from the turning
arrows of our coordinates.

00:29:21.175 --> 00:29:23.350
They're called metric terms.

00:29:23.700 --> 00:29:27.596
With the same recipe,
dotting with j hat and with k hat,

00:29:27.596 --> 00:29:32.675
we get the northward and upward
parts, each with metric terms of its own.

00:29:34.175 --> 00:29:38.267
If you skipped, here's what to keep:
because the arrows turn,

00:29:38.267 --> 00:29:42.493
the wind's numbers can change
even when nothing pushes the air,

00:29:42.493 --> 00:29:46.250
and the extra terms that say
so are called metric terms.

00:29:47.050 --> 00:29:49.375
What do the metric terms mean?

00:29:49.725 --> 00:29:52.150
Let's try a thought experiment.

00:29:52.500 --> 00:29:56.537
Imagine a puck gliding over a smooth
Earth that doesn't spin,

00:29:56.537 --> 00:29:59.250
with nothing pushing it along the ground.

00:29:59.600 --> 00:30:03.225
Then the eastward part
of its acceleration,

00:30:03.225 --> 00:30:06.850
capital D bold v by D
t dot i hat, is zero.

00:30:07.200 --> 00:30:13.396
So capital D u by D t must
equal u v tangent phi over the radius,

00:30:13.396 --> 00:30:15.875
minus u w over the radius.

00:30:16.225 --> 00:30:19.470
The puck stays
on the ground, so w is zero,

00:30:19.470 --> 00:30:24.450
and that leaves u v tangent
phi over the radius, which isn't zero.

00:30:24.800 --> 00:30:29.350
So the puck's eastward number changes,
even though nothing pushes it.

00:30:29.700 --> 00:30:32.659
Let's start it at forty
five degrees north,

00:30:32.659 --> 00:30:36.925
going north-east, at ten metres
per second east and ten north.

00:30:37.275 --> 00:30:41.122
After one day, its east part
has grown to about eleven and

00:30:41.122 --> 00:30:45.300
a half, and its north part has
shrunk to about eight point two.

00:30:46.800 --> 00:30:50.850
But its speed is still
fourteen point one metres per second.

00:30:52.350 --> 00:30:57.225
The puck goes straight, along a great
circle, which we'll meet in Part 6.

00:30:57.575 --> 00:31:00.250
It's our arrows that turned under it.

00:31:00.600 --> 00:31:04.725
Metric terms never speed
anything up or slow it down.

00:31:05.075 --> 00:31:10.325
They only share the same speed out between
east and north, as the arrows turn.

00:31:11.125 --> 00:31:12.825
How big are they?

00:31:13.175 --> 00:31:16.845
Take the same wind, ten
metres per second east and

00:31:16.845 --> 00:31:21.175
ten north, at forty five degrees,
where the tangent is one.

00:31:21.525 --> 00:31:25.872
Let's put these numbers
into u v tangent phi over the radius,

00:31:25.872 --> 00:31:30.575
with the Earth's radius, six point three
seven one million metres.

00:31:30.925 --> 00:31:33.945
That gives about
one point six times ten to

00:31:33.945 --> 00:31:36.825
the minus five metres per second squared.

00:31:38.325 --> 00:31:43.277
Let's compare the Coriolis
effect, from the cross product movies:

00:31:43.277 --> 00:31:46.400
f times v, where f is two Omega sine phi.

00:31:46.750 --> 00:31:49.140
With the Earth's spin rate, Omega,

00:31:49.140 --> 00:31:53.358
seven point two nine times ten
to the minus five per second,

00:31:53.358 --> 00:31:55.819
and the sine of forty five degrees,

00:31:55.819 --> 00:31:58.209
about zero point seven zero seven,

00:31:58.209 --> 00:32:03.200
f is about one point zero three times ten
to the minus four per second.

00:32:03.550 --> 00:32:07.648
Multiplying by the northward
wind, ten metres per second,

00:32:07.648 --> 00:32:11.675
gives about one point zero times ten
to the minus three.

00:32:13.175 --> 00:32:17.100
So the metric term is about
sixty six times smaller.

00:32:18.600 --> 00:32:22.075
In one weather system, metric
terms are small.

00:32:22.425 --> 00:32:26.245
But they grow near the poles, where
the tangent gets large,

00:32:26.245 --> 00:32:29.935
and over flows that span whole
oceans or the whole globe,

00:32:29.935 --> 00:32:32.525
so weather and climate models keep them.

00:32:32.875 --> 00:32:35.697
We'll meet them again in a later movie:

00:32:35.697 --> 00:32:40.400
From F equals mass times acceleration,
to the equation of motion.

00:32:41.200 --> 00:32:46.756
To sum up, a forecaster's local
frame has three arrows: i hat east,

00:32:46.756 --> 00:32:53.225
j hat north and k hat up, and the wind
is u i hat, plus v j hat, plus w k hat.

00:32:53.575 --> 00:32:56.114
Up is the arrow from the Earth's centre,

00:32:56.114 --> 00:32:59.669
east comes from turning
in the view from above the pole,

00:32:59.669 --> 00:33:02.525
and north from turning
in the meridian slice.

00:33:02.875 --> 00:33:05.900
Every place has its own
frame: Brest's up and

00:33:05.900 --> 00:33:10.000
Khulna's up are about seventy
five point eight degrees apart.

00:33:10.350 --> 00:33:14.559
With Part 3's rules, the latitudes
and longitudes of Naples and

00:33:14.559 --> 00:33:17.966
Englewood gave the coast's
two legs, ninety one and

00:33:17.966 --> 00:33:20.905
a half kilometres north
and fifty five west:

00:33:20.905 --> 00:33:23.443
the legs behind the coast's bearing of

00:33:23.443 --> 00:33:26.650
three hundred and twenty
nine degrees in Part 2.

00:33:27.000 --> 00:33:32.750
As the air moves, the arrows turn by
themselves, at speeds divided by radii.

00:33:33.100 --> 00:33:37.022
So the eastward acceleration
is capital D u by D t,

00:33:37.022 --> 00:33:39.944
minus u v tangent phi over the radius,

00:33:39.944 --> 00:33:46.250
plus u w over the radius: two metric terms
that come only from the turning arrows.

00:33:46.600 --> 00:33:48.015
For an ordinary wind,

00:33:48.015 --> 00:33:52.262
they're about sixty six times smaller
than the Coriolis effect,

00:33:52.262 --> 00:33:55.025
but weather and climate models keep them.

00:33:55.375 --> 00:33:58.354
In Part 5, we'll let
the frame itself move,

00:33:58.354 --> 00:34:02.650
and ride along with a storm as it
crosses the English Channel.

00:34:03.000 --> 00:34:08.069
That shows which parts of the storm's
winds come from its own spin, and which

00:34:08.069 --> 00:34:12.875
come only from its motion, and
what a barometer sees as the storm passes.

00:34:13.675 --> 00:34:17.833
This video is one of a series
of related maths tutorials,

00:34:17.833 --> 00:34:19.875
so watch out for the others.

00:34:20.225 --> 00:34:24.622
They're made for students
of atmospheric science, meteorology and

00:34:24.622 --> 00:34:28.275
fluid dynamics, and anyone
else who needs these ideas.

00:34:28.625 --> 00:34:33.453
